# The homepage is served straight from the designers' static file. It used to
# be a React route rendering /marketing/home.html in an <iframe>, which meant
# Google indexed "/" as a document with no text and no headings - iframe
# content is crawled as its own URL and is not credited to the parent page.
#
# The `!` is required: without it Netlify serves the real /index.html on disk
# and never reaches this rule. 200 (rewrite, not redirect) keeps the URL as
# "/". home.html carries <link rel="canonical" href="https://useplanie.com/">
# so the /marketing/home.html URL does not compete with it.
/            /marketing/home.html   200!

# One homepage URL, not two.
/index.html  /                      301!

# Single-page app fallback. React Router owns /waitlist, /privacy, /contact and
# friends client-side, but Netlify only has index.html on disk — without this,
# a direct hit or refresh on any of those paths returns Netlify's 404 page.
# Real files (assets, /marketing/*) still win over this rule. Rewrite targets
# are served as-is and not re-matched against these rules, so the /index.html
# redirect above does not fire for them.
/*  /index.html  200
